ration is essential for building secure systems. Localized telemetry and market-driven insurance pools can price real deployment risks without banning the underlying foundation code.\n\nThe political choice is clear: either we protect decentralized innovation or we engineer an artificial cloud cartel. Closed-API vendors benefit when regulators outlaw open-weight distribution under the guise of upstream enterprise liability. Independent developers, public hospitals, and small startups bear the full economic cost. If we destroy open-access foundation models, we forfeit the distributed trial-and-error that automates medical discovery and eliminates scarcity. Regulators should enforce tort remedies against negligent deployers at the point of impact, not criminalize the distribution of general-purpose computing.",
