  "statement": "Mandating commercial liability insurance cannot replace architectural safeguards because underwriters cannot price non-deterministic risks without deterministic circuit breakers. Opponents argue that requiring large balance-sheet reserves and commercial insurance policies will deter reckless deployments more effectively than procedural checklists. That view correctly recognizes that corporate actors only respect direct financial exposure. Underwriters cannot calculate premiums for autonomous models that lack verified operational boundaries. Actuarial science requires historical failure data and deterministic limits. Without an out-of-band supervisor capping system permissions, insurers face unbounded liability and will refuse coverage entirely.\n\nAutomated supervisor logs cannot serve as an exculpatory shield against strict product liability claims. In tort law, strict design defect liability evaluates whether the product's design caused unreasonable danger, not whether the deployer exercised procedural due care. The Boeing 737 MAX litigation demonstrated that internal compliance documentation cannot defeat design defect claims when an automated flight control system lacks redundant fail-safes. Under the Restatement (Third) of Torts, plaintiffs defeat summary judgment by proving a reasonable alternative design was commercially available. An out-of-band supervisor that halts unauthorized database writes is an available engineering design. Disabling or omitting that supervisor establishes prima facie proof of a defective product.\n\nSafety supervisors operate as deterministic execution gates rather than internal statistical mind-readers. As documented in \"The Rush to Adopt AI: Business Risks & How to Get it Right,\" autonomous tools require direct write access to enterprise data repositories across corporate networks. A system's damage potential scales directly with the breadth of its operational permissions. An active safety supervisor intercepts unauthorized API calls, enforces access boundaries, and freezes execution during severe distribution shifts. In July 2024, a voltage fluctuation in northern Virginia disconnected 60 data centers simultaneously because industrial electrical relays functioned as physical circuit breakers. Software systems controlling enterprise infrastructure require identical physical and logic gates.\n\nCongress and state attorneys general must condition commercial deployment rights on verified runtime circuit breakers and financial insurance floors. Enterprise deployers currently capture massive operational profits while shifting the systemic blast radius onto consumers and infrastructure operators. A bipartisan coalition of consumer protection advocates and liability insurers supports strict boundary enforcement to ensure risk calculability. This framework relies on the key assumption that autonomous agents will execute high-consequence API commands without continuous human review. Denying this standard leaves society defenseless against automated cascade failures.",
